        "original_id": "84b60705-bf72-5e1f-b964-51cfe0797eaa",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Game of the Goose, Medina, The Will of an Eccentric\n- People: Jules Verne\n- Places: Medina, Atlas Mountains\n- Concepts: board games, player counts, dice, adventure novels\n\nFacts:\n- In 1900, Jules Verne wrote The Will of an Eccentric, an adventure novel based on the Game of the Goose.\n- The Game of the Goose is a board game in which two or more players move pieces around a track by rolling a die.\n- Medina is a board game set in 1822 in a desert city near the Atlas Mountains called Medina.\n- In Medina, three or four players compete to become the most influential developer of Medina.\n- Variations of Medina allow 2 or 5 players.",
